  "tips": "Arabic has influenced Hebrew in every domain.\n\nFrom food (**פלאפל**, **חומוס**, **טחינה**) to slang (**יאללה**, **אחי**, **כיף**), Arabic loan words are woven into everyday Israeli Hebrew. Some are used widely by all speakers, while others are more common in casual speech.\n\n**יאללה** (from Arabic يلا) is perhaps the most common — used to mean 'let's go,' 'come on,' or even 'okay, bye.' **כיף** (from كيف, 'pleasure') simply means 'fun' in Hebrew. **זבאלה** and **חאפלה** are considered informal slang."
